# Pre-push quality gate

Do **not** `git push` (especially to `main` / `master`) while checks are failing or were not run.

## Before push

1. Read `.github/workflows/ci.yml` in this repo — run the same steps locally.
2. Fix failures in the same session, or stop **without** pushing.
3. Push only when local checks pass (or you have verified CI would pass).

## Typical commands

| Repo type | Run before push |
|-----------|-----------------|
| Python NAS / hub | `python -m ruff check .` then `python -m pytest -q` |
| homey-guest-relay | `npm test` and `npm run build` |
| lepuy-location | `npm run lint` and `npm run build` |
| homey-scripts | no CI — still run any relevant script checks before push |

Use `python -m ruff` when `ruff` is not on PATH (common on Windows). Install deps from `requirements-dev.txt` or `npm ci` — do not push hoping CI will catch missing packages.

## Agents

- Do not push broken work to "let CI find it."
- Do not push a follow-up fix for a failure you introduced unless the user asked to babysit CI.
- Ship `VERSION` + `CHANGELOG` bumps in the same commit as passing checks.
